{"availability":"available","full":"rovelstars/rasmalai","name":"rasmalai","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-02T04:32:38Z","updated":"2026-10-04T07:55:04Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://rasmalai.rovelstars.com/playground","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:01.385Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:01.385Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:01.385Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:16:01.385Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Documentation · Issues · Website · View packages","Rasmalai is a high-performance compiled programming language. It pairs TypeScript-like developer ergonomics with native C-ABI interop, a multi-pass LIR optimizer, a Cranelift JIT for fast dev cycles, and an LLVM AOT backend for release builds. One toolchain covers scripting, native binaries, and a browser playground.","Mainstream systems languages force a choice: ergonomics or control. Rasmalai refuses it — memory safety through ARC with explicit cyclic edges instead of a garbage collector, Python-grade readability with native execution speed, and a standard library that treats files, sockets, threads, and SIMD as first-class citizens rather than FFI afterthoughts."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rovelstars/rasmalai/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4cd224349d39bbe5f5e7e190b09a642b66a0b5d6a1e05684f3dc151f8c09e564","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:37.813Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:37.813Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Documentation · Issues · Website · View packages","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rovelstars/rasmalai/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"4cd224349d39bbe5f5e7e190b09a642b66a0b5d6a1e05684f3dc151f8c09e564","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rovelstars/rasmalai/blo